[description]

This package provides an in-memory store for [term geo/point] definitions, which groups points
lying close to each other on the map into clusters.

[para] The base data is pulled from a backing store, a [package map::point::store::fs] or any other
object providing the API described in section [term {Store API}] of
[package map::point::store::fs]. All points are loaded from the backing store at creation, and their
pixel coordinates and clusters are computed for all zoom levels from [const 0] up to a given
maximum. It is the store expected by [package map::point::map-display], and can also be used with
[package map::point::table-display].

[para] The clustering is computed with a simple algorithm whose run time grows quadratically with
the number of points. The package is intended for demonstration, and for small to medium sets of
points.

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [cmd ::map::point::store::memory] [arg storeName] [arg store] [arg maxzoom]]

Creates a new store object named [arg storeName] on top of the backing store [arg store], and
returns the fully qualified name of its command. The [arg storeName] can be [const %AUTO%] to
generate a unique name.

[para] The [arg store] is the name of the command of the backing store, an object providing the
methods [method ids] and [method get] as described in section [term {Store API}] of
[package map::point::store::fs]. It is not destroyed together with the memory store.

[para] All points of the backing store are loaded, and their pixel coordinates and clusters are
computed for the zoom levels [const 0] to [arg maxzoom]. The latter should be the highest zoom
level of the map the points are shown in, i.e. the number of levels of the map's tile provider minus
one. Later changes to the backing store are not seen.

[para] At zoom levels below [const 18] points which are within a few tens of pixels of each other
are grouped into a [term cluster], shown in their place. At zoom level [const 18] and above no
clustering is done.

[call [arg storeName] [method ids]]

Returns the list of the ids of all [term geo/point]s. Clusters are not included. This method is
delegated to the backing store.

[call [arg storeName] [method visible] [arg geobox] [arg zoom]]

Returns the list of the ids of the points and clusters to show at the given [arg zoom] level, which
are located inside the geographical box [arg geobox] (a list of minimal latitude, minimal longitude,
maximal latitude and maximal longitude). The points which are members of a cluster at this zoom
level are not included, the cluster is reported instead. The [arg zoom] level must be in the range
[const 0] to [arg maxzoom], otherwise an error is thrown.

[call [arg storeName] [method get] [arg id]]

Returns the attributes of the point or cluster with the given [arg id], a dictionary. Throws an
error if the [arg id] is not known.

[para] For a point it contains all the keys returned by the backing store, i.e. at least
[const names], [const kind], and [const geo] (see [package map::point::file]), extended with the
key [const bbox], the geographical box of the point (minimal and maximal coordinates both equal to
the location).

[para] The ids of clusters have the form [const c/][var N], where [var N] is a number. Each cluster
belongs to a single zoom level. For a cluster the dictionary contains the keys:

[list_begin definitions]
[def [const names]] An empty list.
[def [const kind]]  The string [const cluster].
[def [const geo]]   The location of the center of the cluster, a list of latitude and longitude.
[def [const count]] The number of points in the cluster.
[list_end]

[call [arg storeName] [method pixels] [arg id] [arg zoom]]

Returns the location of the point or cluster with the given [arg id] in pixel coordinates of the
map at the given [arg zoom] level, a list of x and y coordinates (see [package map::slippy]). For a
point the [arg zoom] level must be in the range [const 0] to [arg maxzoom], for a cluster it must be
the zoom level the cluster belongs to. Otherwise an error is thrown.

[call [arg storeName] [method destroy]]

Destroys the store.

[list_end]

[para] All other methods are delegated to the backing store as well.

[para] The methods [method ids], [method get], [method visible], and [method pixels] are the API
used by [package map::point::map-display]. [package map::point::table-display] uses only
[method ids] and [method get]. Any object providing these methods with the same results can be used
in place of a [package map::point::store::memory].

[section EXAMPLE]

[example_begin]
package require map::point::store::fs
package require map::point::store::memory

map point store fs     PointFiles /path/to/directory
map point store memory Points     PointFiles 18

# What to show of the whole world at zoom level 3
foreach id [lb]Points visible {-85 -180 85 180} 3[rb] {
    set point [lb]Points get $id[rb]
    if {[lb]dict get $point kind[rb] eq "cluster"} {
        puts "cluster of [lb]dict get $point count[rb] points at [lb]Points pixels $id 3[rb]"
    } else {
        puts "[lb]join [lb]dict get $point names[rb] {, }[rb] at [lb]Points pixels $id 3[rb]"
    }
}
[example_end]

